(>> 1.2 Fluid Mosaic Model of Biological Membranes) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(Proposed by S.J. Singer and Garth L. Nicolson in 1972, the Fluid Mosaic Model remains) Tj
T*
(the universal foundation for membrane structure.) Tj
T*
(* Lipid Bilayer Matrix: Amphipathic phospholipids spontaneously assemble into a) Tj
T*
(continuous bilayer in aqueous media. Polar hydrophilic headgroups \(glycerol backbone) Tj
T*
(esterified to phosphate and choline/ethanolamine\) orient toward the intra- and) Tj
T*
(extracellular fluids, while hydrophobic nonpolar fatty acid tails \(saturated and) Tj
T*
(cis-unsaturated hydrocarbon chains\) pack into the hydrophobic core.) Tj
T*
(* Membrane Fluidity Regulators: Fluidity is determined by fatty acid saturation and) Tj
T*
(temperature. Cis-double bonds create 30-degree kinks preventing dense crystalline) Tj
T*
(packing, lowering the phase-transition temperature \(Tm\). In animal cells, cholesterol) Tj
T*
(acts as a bidirectional fluidity buffer: at physiological temperatures \(37 deg C\),) Tj
T*
(its rigid steroid planar rings restrain phospholipid lateral movement, reducing) Tj
T*
(permeability; at low temperatures, it prevents close hydrocarbon tail packing,) Tj
T*
(preventing membrane crystallization.) Tj
T*
(* Membrane Asymmetry: The inner \(cytosolic\) and outer \(exoplasmic\) leaflets exhibit) Tj
T*
(distinct lipid compositions. Phosphatidylcholine and sphingomyelin predominate in the) Tj
T*
(outer leaflet, whereas phosphatidylethanolamine and negatively charged) Tj
T*
(phosphatidylserine are concentrated in the inner leaflet. Flip-flop \(transverse\)) Tj
T*
(movement between leaflets is thermodynamically unfavored and catalyzed by) Tj
T*
