(Problem Context: Digitalis and ouabain are plant-derived cardiotonic steroids used) Tj
T*
(clinically in congestive heart failure. Explain the molecular cascade and calculate why) Tj
T*
(inhibiting the primary active Na+/K+ pump enhances cardiac muscle contraction velocity.) Tj
T*
(Step 1 \(Pump Inhibition\): Digitalis binds stereospecifically to the extracellular pocket) Tj
T*
(of the phosphorylated E2-P conformation of Na+/K+ ATPase, halting ATP-dependent) Tj
T*
(dephosphorylation and pump recycling.) Tj
T*
(Step 2 \(Intracellular Sodium Elevation\): Because primary Na+ extrusion is diminished) Tj
T*
(while Na+ leak channels remain functional, cytosolic [Na+] rises from baseline ~10 mM to) Tj
T*
(~25 mM, dissipating the steep transmembrane Na+ concentration gradient.) Tj
T*
(Step 3 \(Secondary Active Transporter Suppression\): The cardiac sarcolemmal 3Na+/1Ca2+) Tj
T*
(antiporter \(NCX\) relies on the free energy of downhill Na+ influx to drive uphill Ca2+) Tj
T*
(extrusion. The reduced chemical potential gradient of Na+ dramatically reduces the) Tj
T*
(driving force for Ca2+ efflux or causes reverse mode operation.) Tj
T*
(Step 4 \(Sarcoplasmic Reticulum Loading\): Elevated cytosolic [Ca2+] is sequestered by the) Tj
T*
(SERCA2a pump into the sarcoplasmic reticulum. Upon subsequent electrical depolarization,) Tj
T*
(an amplified burst of Ca2+ is released through Ryanodine receptors into the myoplasm.) Tj
T*
(Conclusion: Ca2+ binds Troponin C with higher saturation, promoting stronger) Tj
T*
(actin-myosin cross-bridge cycling and inducing positive inotropic myocardial) Tj
T*
(contractility.) Tj
