(Problem Context: In the brush border membrane of intestinal epithelial cells, the SGLT1) Tj
T*
(cotransporter moves 1 molecule of D-glucose into the cell coupled to the influx of 2 Na+) Tj
T*
(ions. Derive the thermodynamic equation and determine whether an extracellular [Na+] of) Tj
T*
(140 mM, intracellular [Na+] of 14 mM, and membrane potential of -70 mV can accumulate) Tj
T*
(glucose inside the cell against a 1,000-fold concentration gradient at 37 deg C \(310 K\).) Tj
T*
(Thermodynamic Relation: For 2 Na+ coupled transport, free energy change delta G = delta) Tj
T*
(G_glucose + 2 * delta G_Na.) Tj
T*
(At equilibrium, delta G = 0: delta G_glucose = -2 * delta G_Na.) Tj
T*
(delta G_glucose = R * T * ln\([Glucose_in] / [Glucose_out]\)) Tj
T*
(delta G_Na = R * T * ln\([Na_in] / [Na_out]\) + z * F * Vm) Tj
T*
(Values: R = 8.314 J/mol*K, T = 310 K, F = 96485 C/mol, Vm = -0.070 V, [Na_in]/[Na_out] =) Tj
T*
(14/140 = 0.1, z = +1.) Tj
T*
(Calculation of Electrochemical Energy per mol Na+:) Tj
T*
(delta G_Na = \(8.314 * 310 * ln\(0.1\)\) + \(1 * 96485 * \(-0.070\)\)) Tj
T*
(delta G_Na = \(2577.34 * \(-2.3026\)\) - 6753.95 = -5934.57 - 6753.95 = -12,688.5 J/mol =) Tj
T*
(-12.69 kJ/mol.) Tj
